{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 1 - REBAR FAILURE MODES OBSERVED, all from judge adjudications. (1) RECALL, NOT PRECISION, is the weakness: 201 missed TPs against 61 unique, and only 2 of the 201 are genuine gaps. The rest are misses where a criterion exists and stays silent. (2) ROUTING: on 62d9-9f6d-BLOCK rebar's A1 finding enumerated the correct evidence AND prescribed exactly the fix CE and mini prescribed, then filed it at severity:none, priority:0.0. It had the answer and scored it at zero. (3) SELF-CORROBORATION inflating a false positive: on bda8-370d-BLOCK rebar claimed add_issues_to_epic raises NotImplementedError before any HTTP call; in jira 3.10.5 the method POSTs with no guard and that string appears nowhere in the package. rebar then cited its OWN plan-review cache as corroborating evidence, turning 1 error into 3 rows, 2 of them blocking. The disproof was already on the ticket it was reviewing. (4) DUPLICATION: +49 net merged rows, the only arm that emits one issue under several criteria; on 62d9-9f6d-BLOCK 11 rows were 8 distinct issues, overstating by 38%. (5) DETECTED-THEN-WITHDRAWN: on bda8-370d-BLOCK 3 of 13 missed issues were found and then suppressed below threshold."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000803442667001,"uuid":"7eab8f34-f5a9-4972-ad6b-79bb56c36012"}